<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Tudor</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tudor dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Tudor was the royal family of Welsh origin that ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and Ireland from 1485 to 1603. Its monarchs were Henry VII, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a>, Edward VI, Mary I and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I</a>. Their reigns saw the English <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a>, the growth of royal government, the conquest and shiring of Ireland, and the beginnings of English overseas expansion.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-tudor.jpg" alt="House of Tudor" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tudor_Rose.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Henry Tudor took the crown as Henry VII, founding the <b>Tudor dynasty</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/august-22">22 August in history</a></li><li><blockquote>The treaty helped secure the new <b>Tudor dynasty</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/november-3">3 November in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Under the <b>Tudors</b> the area became County Cavan in 1584.</blockquote><a href="/state/east-breifne">East Breifne</a></li></ul></section>
